WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.200
After meeting the adult Andy Barclay during&nbsp;
the post-credits scene of the last movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:06.000
we’re now introduced to his snowy&nbsp;
cabin, which gives us little clues&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.520
about how his character developed in the&nbsp;
14 year absence after Child’s Play 3.

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:11.920
It’s obvious that he made himself&nbsp;
a hunter, and sports an impressive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:15.440
collection of firearms. Between that and&nbsp;
this framed sweater from Kent Academy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:19.200
the military school he attended as a teen, it’s&nbsp;
safe to say that his time at the school had a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:23.760
profound effect on him. The latin text at the&nbsp;
bottom of the garment says Nunquam Non Paratus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:28.080
which translates to: Never Unprepared -- a&nbsp;
perfect description of Andy if I ever saw one.

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:32.160
Behind this frame is a secret safe. We only&nbsp;
see him punch in part of the combination,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:34.880
if we assume that each number on&nbsp;
the keypad has a unique touchtone,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:39.520
then we can use sound to figure out&nbsp;
what the full combination is: 110011,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:44.400
which is binary for the number: 3. Kent Academy&nbsp;
is the setting of Child’s Play 3, and Cult of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:48.960
Chucky is the first sequel to Andy’s story in&nbsp;
Child’s Play 3, twenty-six years in the making.

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:52.080
It’s probably also no coincidence that&nbsp;
the spare Good Guy doll that Andy keeps&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:55.600
has short hair. This not only helps Andy&nbsp;
differentiate his doll from the others,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:58.400
but also might be a nod to the fact&nbsp;
that he and the other cadets were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:02.560
forced to maintain short hair at the academy.&nbsp;
Additionally, during one bizarre dream scene,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:07.440
Nica sees this image of Chucky flash before&nbsp;
her eyes. This is Chucky from Child’s Play 3.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:11.200
Nica was not there for Child’s Play 3,&nbsp;
so this has to be for us, the audience.

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:14.320
To learn how one character in this movie&nbsp;
might have been connected to the main&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:17.840
character from the Chucky TV series,&nbsp;
stick around to the end of this video.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:20.726
(metal music intro)

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:28.160
Guess what? You’ve been involuntarily&nbsp;
committed to another episode of Things&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:29.760
You Missed. The only way to get out of it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:33.840
is if you need to watch the previous episodes.&nbsp;
As of posting, I’ve covered every Chucky movie.

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:37.600
Cult of Chucky came on the heels of the&nbsp;
darker, more serious Curse of Chucky. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:41.600
despite having a similar visual style and&nbsp;
bringing back Curse’s protagonist -- Cult&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:45.680
kind of falls back to the old ways of&nbsp;
facetious jokes and overt references.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:49.040
Through the good and the bad, I’ll be here&nbsp;
to guide you through some of the things you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:53.484
may have missed. So let us get in -- to&nbsp;
some of the things you may have missed.

00:01:53.484 --> 00:01:58.124
(mysterious high quality music)

00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:02.160
The film opens with Andy on a date, and it&nbsp;
definitely feels like a conscious choice that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:06.560
he’s chosen a red-head woman after living&nbsp;
a life of PTSD from this red-headed doll.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:10.000
It’s possible that Nica, who was also&nbsp;
tortured by Chucky, befell the same fate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:12.480
based on this off-color joke&nbsp;
from her fellow inmate Malcolm.

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:14.400
– You still have a thing for red-heads?

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:18.960
– However, it is not long into the date that Andy&nbsp;
realizes she’s aware of his tumultuous past.

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:20.400
– You Googled me.

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:24.000
– Oh, so Google does exist in this world?&nbsp;
I only bring it up because they went to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:28.000
extreme lengths in the last movie to specify&nbsp;
that the search engine Nica uses is called&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:31.440
“Internet Search”. And perhaps&nbsp;
stranger still, later in this movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:35.520
we find out that Andy uploads content on&nbsp;
the famous social media site: “Video”.

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:39.040
The date doesn’t work out, so Andy finds&nbsp;
himself home and cracking open a drink from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:43.120
fridge. The brand of choice is called “Blady’s”,&nbsp;
perhaps a reference to Chucky’s favorite weapon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:46.960
his trusty blade. Yeah, Andy’s on that&nbsp;
beer and mayonnaise diet right now.

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:50.320
Andy’s safe contains a captured Chucky&nbsp;
head, who, despite his situation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:52.480
tries to bite Andy, prompting him to ask…

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:53.440
– You wanna play?

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:57.200
– …Which is one of the phrases that the original&nbsp;
Good Guy doll says in the original movie.

00:02:57.200 --> 00:02:59.040
– Hey, wanna play?

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:02.640
– This is not the only time that Cult of&nbsp;
Chucky echoes lines from the past. During&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:06.480
the group therapy session at the psychiatric&nbsp;
hospital we hear one of the patients say…

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:07.200
– Chucky did it.

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:10.480
– [Zac] … a line that Andy learned&nbsp;
not to say a long time ago..

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:11.643
– Chucky did it.

00:03:11.643 --> 00:03:13.495
– [Tommy Pickles] You did it Chucky!

00:03:13.495 --> 00:03:15.200
– [Chucky Finster] Yeah, I did!

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:19.280
– So he admits it! Of course, this wouldn’t be a&nbsp;
post-Scream Chucky movie if there weren’t some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:23.120
kind of franchise callback every 5 minutes or&nbsp;
so. Let's make sure we’ve got them all covered.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:27.680
Anyone mind if we start with Child’s&nbsp;
Play 1? Oh, you do mind? Well too bad!

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:31.360
At the beginning we see Nica receiving some kind&nbsp;
of shock therapy. OK, I don’t even know if that’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:35.280
supposed to be a callback, but it’s just nice to&nbsp;
see that they invented a shock therapy device that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:39.440
doesn’t kill you since that… uh… unfortunate&nbsp;
Dr. Ardmore incident in the first movie.

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:43.040
After the treatment, one of the doctors&nbsp;
pricks Nica with a needle and says…

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:47.120
See? From the waist down she’s a pin cushion.
Another form of pin cushion is a voodoo doll,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:49.440
perhaps a reference to the fact that&nbsp;
Charles Lee Ray obtained the power&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:52.880
to supernaturally possess a doll using&nbsp;
the art of voodoo in the first movie.

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:55.920
Later on, when Chucky has infiltrated&nbsp;
the hospital, he finds himself alone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:59.120
with one of the patients, Claire, who is&nbsp;
strapped down to a hospital bed. The way&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:02.880
Chucky scurries around her before taking her&nbsp;
out is very similar to how he circles Mike&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:06.720
Norris’s crashed car in the original. When I&nbsp;
covered that first film on Things You Missed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:11.040
I talked about how I found this Good Guy mascot&nbsp;
to be way creepier than the actual Chucky doll.

00:04:12.720 --> 00:04:17.120
“Look at this thing. Imagine this chasing after&nbsp;
you in a dark alley. Would have been way better.”

00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:20.720
Well, I kind of got my wish in Cult,&nbsp;
during Nica’s dream / hallucination&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:24.000
scene -- although instead of a dark alley&nbsp;
it’s a bright hallway. But seeing this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:27.840
giant Chucky is probably my favorite part of&nbsp;
this movie. Also, take a closer look at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:31.520
reflection in the Giant Chucky’s knife.&nbsp;
This is the human form Charles Lee Ray,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:35.120
who we’ve seen in the original movie,&nbsp;
and in flashbacks during Curse of Chucky.

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:39.120
Finally, the story in Cult ends with Andy&nbsp;
voluntarily entering the asylum to try to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:42.400
save Nica, but he ends up locked in&nbsp;
solitary confinement as a result.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:45.280
This isn’t the first time he’s been&nbsp;
here, as way back in Child’s Play,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:48.480
he was locked up in a children’s mental&nbsp;
facility, and the way he slides into a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:51.840
sitting position against the wall mimics&nbsp;
the exact response he had back then.

00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:54.240
But that’s just the Child’s Play 1 references.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:57.520
We’ve still gotta talk about all the secrets&nbsp;
linking Cult to the rest of the franchise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.520 --> 00:05:01.155
the hidden text on these tombstones&nbsp;
and the rest of the Things You Missed.

00:05:01.256 --> 00:05:03.256
(impact)

00:05:06.132 --> 00:05:08.132
(eerie music)

00:05:09.920 --> 00:05:13.360
When the Chucky cult has expanded to three&nbsp;
different dolls, they start to interact with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.360 --> 00:05:17.840
each other, and share their love of being a serial&nbsp;
criminal. Chucky refers to this as “his job”,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.840 --> 00:05:21.619
which I don’t fully understand, because he’s&nbsp;
not getting paid for it, as far as I can tell.

00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:29.040
– And I love my job. Especially the look&nbsp;
on my victim's face when they realize,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:35.600
in that final moment, that it's all really&nbsp;
happening. A children's toy is actually beating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:42.480
them to death with a yardstick! Or setting them&nbsp;
on fire. Eviscerating them. All actual examples.

00:05:42.480 --> 00:05:46.240
– We’ve seen a couple of these. The yardstick is&nbsp;
from Child’s Play 2, where Chucky gives Andy’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:50.160
schoolteacher a little after school punishment.&nbsp;
The fire comes from Bride of Chucky, where we see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:54.800
him set a cop car ablaze. I don't really know who&nbsp;
he eviscerated. It could be an off-screen death.&nbsp;

00:05:54.800 --> 00:05:58.240
There are a lot of other Bride of Chucky&nbsp;
references though. For example when Claire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.240 --> 00:06:01.840
is restrained on the hospital bed, he&nbsp;
uses an oxygen tank to shatter the glass&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:05.200
ceiling above her, and it is actually&nbsp;
the falling glass shards that do her in.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.200 --> 00:06:08.720
This is effectively the same kill as the one&nbsp;
that Tiffany committed at the honeymoon suite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:12.400
motel in Niagara Falls, where she throws a&nbsp;
champagne bottle at a mirror on the ceiling.

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:15.760
The main concept of Cult revolves around&nbsp;
Chucky’s new ability to inhabit more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:15.760 --> 00:06:19.520
than one body at once. He claims the&nbsp;
spell comes from VoodooForDummies.com,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:22.480
the online version of the spellbook&nbsp;
that Tiffany uses in Bride.

00:06:22.480 --> 00:06:26.240
At one point we see three Chucky dolls all&nbsp;
possessed by Charles Lee Ray’s soul at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:29.760
same time, and when Nurse Carlos comes&nbsp;
into the room and sees what’s going on,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.760 --> 00:06:33.360
all of their heads turn simultaneously to&nbsp;
face him. The short haired Chucky’s head&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.360 --> 00:06:37.840
does a 180° spin, something that we saw in
Bride and nearly every entry since.

00:06:37.840 --> 00:06:41.120
There’s another Bride reference not long&nbsp;
after, when Tiff arrives and slits the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.120 --> 00:06:44.560
throat of a cop from behind. This one&nbsp;
might actually just be a security guard,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.560 --> 00:06:47.600
I’m not really sure, but this is the&nbsp;
third time we’ve seen her do this.

00:06:47.600 --> 00:06:52.240
– Some things never change though.
– A true classic never goes out of style.

00:06:52.240 --> 00:06:55.200
– The one movie that doesn’t get a&nbsp;
lot of love in Cult, thankfully,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:59.040
is Seed. When I talked about Seed, I mentioned&nbsp;
how the opening is very similar to the opening&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.040 --> 00:07:03.760
of Halloween. A little bit of Chucky paying homage&nbsp;
to a slasher forefather. Cult also has a beginning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.760 --> 00:07:07.760
that is similar to Halloween, just for the fact&nbsp;
that very early on we see a patient transfer.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:11.040
Several Halloween movies have a patient&nbsp;
transfer at the beginning. In particular,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:14.640
Halloween 4 begins with Michel Myers&nbsp;
being moved to a lower security hospital,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.640 --> 00:07:18.640
which is exactly what we see happening to&nbsp;
Nica when we first see her character in Cult.

00:07:18.640 --> 00:07:22.000
Finally, we have the last movie, Curse&nbsp;
of Chucky. There’s not much in terms of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:25.600
Things You might have Missed, since, come&nbsp;
on, this was only one movie ago. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.600 --> 00:07:29.200
when we first see Nica at the cafeteria in&nbsp;
Harrogate Hospital, the scene opens with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.200 --> 00:07:32.880
a top-down shot on this bowl, it’s gotta be&nbsp;
a call back to the dinner scene from Curse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.880 --> 00:07:36.640
which used the same camera angle and left the&nbsp;
audience to guess whose meal was poisoned.

00:07:36.640 --> 00:07:41.200
In addition to its connections to Chucky movies of&nbsp;
past, there also seem to be links to the future.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.200 --> 00:07:43.440
That’s right, I’m talking about the Chucky series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:46.240
Season 1, but I’m gonna come&nbsp;
back to that later in the video.

00:07:46.240 --> 00:07:50.400
First, I want to take a closer look at the opening&nbsp;
title sequence. Because we haven’t done that yet.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.400 --> 00:07:54.240
We are shown various headlines recapping the&nbsp;
events of Curse. If you look at the author of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:58.400
this one, it says LaDonna Kettell Bonham. This&nbsp;
is probably a family member of Jermy Bonham,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.400 --> 00:08:01.440
who is listed in the movie’s credits&nbsp;
as the animator of the main title sequence.

00:08:01.440 --> 00:08:04.800
The other one is by Surya Cassidy.&nbsp;
I’m guessing if you switch those words&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.800 --> 00:08:09.040
around to say Cassidy Surya, you have the&nbsp;
wife of the title designer, Martin Surya.

00:08:09.040 --> 00:08:12.960
The hospital has it’s own graveyard on site, and&nbsp;
there are a bunch more crew reference easter eggs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.960 --> 00:08:16.880
including Costume Designer Patricia J&nbsp;
Henderson, property master Mark Stratton,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.880 --> 00:08:20.640
assistant production coordinator Aaron Graham,&nbsp;
assistant set decorator Robert Kestler,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.640 --> 00:08:24.240
accounting clerk Heather Wiebe (deep breath) payroll accountant Tracey Phillips -- first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.240 --> 00:08:28.080
assistant director Douglas Mitchell, accounting&nbsp;
clerk Tammy Gibson and art department coordinator&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.080 --> 00:08:31.200
Donna Jenkyns. Yeah, there are always a&nbsp;
lot of crew reference easter eggs when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.200 --> 00:08:35.200
we’re dealing with gravestones and memorials; I&nbsp;
learned that from my Final Destination videos.

00:08:35.200 --> 00:08:38.800
Now if you’ve seen my videos on Bride and&nbsp;
Seed, you know that that’s when Chucky was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.800 --> 00:08:43.040
very inspired by the Scream franchise and it’s&nbsp;
metacinema tendencies. I explained how each of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.040 --> 00:08:46.640
those movies does it’s own take on a classic&nbsp;
horror film, with Bride of Chucky obviously&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.640 --> 00:08:50.240
doing Bride of Frankenstein, and Seed of&nbsp;
Chucky doing Alfred Hitchcock’s Psycho.

00:08:50.240 --> 00:08:52.720
Here in Cult of Chucky, one of&nbsp;
the mental patients, Madeline,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:52.720 --> 00:08:55.840
believes that the Chucky doll is her&nbsp;
baby during an episode of schizophrenia.

00:08:55.840 --> 00:08:58.560
– [Chucky] I’m your friend to the end!
– [Madeline] You know Chucky,&nbsp;

00:08:58.560 --> 00:09:00.960
a boy’s best friend is his mother.

00:09:00.960 --> 00:09:03.600
– If you’ve seen Psycho, you&nbsp;
probably recognize that line.

00:09:03.600 --> 00:09:05.840
– Well, a boy’s best friend is his mother.

00:09:05.840 --> 00:09:09.600
– But it would be a different movie that served&nbsp;
as kind of the base movie for Cult of Chucky,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:09.600 --> 00:09:13.920
only this time, it wouldn’t be a horror movie.&nbsp;
Early on, Nica receives a pack of Juicy Fruit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:13.920 --> 00:09:18.800
gum from this nurse. This brings to mind a well&nbsp;
known scene from the 1975 film One Flew Over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:18.800 --> 00:09:22.640
The Cuckoo’s Nest, where the main character,&nbsp;
McMurphy, offers his seemingly mute in-mate some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.640 --> 00:09:26.880
Juicy Fruit, which leads to him discovering that&nbsp;
he was faking it, he actually can hear and speak.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.880 --> 00:09:31.200
Nica’s situation at Harrogate is kind of similar,&nbsp;
only she’s not really faking it, she was actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.200 --> 00:09:35.040
forced to believe that she’s crazy because&nbsp;
nobody else will believe that Chucky is alive.

00:09:35.040 --> 00:09:38.320
The character Madeline also tries to snuff&nbsp;
Chucky out with a pillow at one point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:38.320 --> 00:09:41.280
which is something that also happens&nbsp;
in One Flew Over The Cuckoo’s Nest,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.280 --> 00:09:44.480
I’m not gonna spoil it. If those two&nbsp;
scenes aren’t proof enough that Harrogate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.480 --> 00:09:48.320
is based on the hospital from One Flew, Chucky&nbsp;
basically calls it out when he shows up there.

00:09:48.320 --> 00:09:51.600
– [Chucky] Jesus! F***ing cuckoo's nest. 

00:09:51.600 --> 00:09:54.960
– Believe it or not, that isn’t the&nbsp;
most obvious reference in the movie.

00:09:54.960 --> 00:09:59.120
– You sound like Hannibal Lecter. Can't&nbsp;
believe they canceled that show.

00:09:59.120 --> 00:10:01.760
– I guess the story there is that the&nbsp;
creator of Child’s Play and Chucky,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.760 --> 00:10:05.040
Don Mancini, worked on the Hannibal&nbsp;
TV series during its final season,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:09.200
so he was upset when the show got canceled.&nbsp;
However, I guess that his short time on that show ended&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:13.200
up inspiring him to bring Chucky to the small&nbsp;
screen -- so maybe it all worked out in the end.

00:10:13.200 --> 00:10:16.560
Speaking of which, as Dr. Foley and Nurse&nbsp;
Carlos are treating one of the patients,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.560 --> 00:10:21.120
they engage in a little small talk, which contains&nbsp;
an interesting and potentially significant detail.

00:10:21.120 --> 00:10:25.555
(impact)

00:10:26.545 --> 00:10:29.793
(dark cinematic music)

00:10:30.400 --> 00:10:33.920
One interesting aspect of Cult of Chucky&nbsp;
is the fact that the killer dolls are not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:33.920 --> 00:10:37.920
the only bad guys in this film. There’s&nbsp;
also the abusive psychiatrist, Dr. Foley,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:37.920 --> 00:10:41.840
who hypnotizes Nica so that she cannot remember&nbsp;
their sessions. During one of these sessions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:41.840 --> 00:10:44.800
you can spot Chucky’s shoes peeking out&nbsp;
from behind a curtain in the background&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:44.800 --> 00:10:48.400
as a clue that the possessed Good Guy&nbsp;
doll would be intervening before long.

00:10:48.400 --> 00:10:51.680
It’s not until later in the movie that we&nbsp;
learn Chucky can inhabit multiple bodies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:51.680 --> 00:10:55.680
but there is a clue in Madeline’s room. She&nbsp;
has drawn many sketches of the Chucky doll,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:55.680 --> 00:10:58.960
and one of them has eyes with huge&nbsp;
pupils, which in the previous films,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:58.960 --> 00:11:02.720
is what happens when Chucky comes to life,&nbsp;
meaning that Madeline has seen this happen.

00:11:02.720 --> 00:11:05.440
If you’re paying close attention&nbsp;
to the calendar date of each event,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:05.440 --> 00:11:09.840
you may have also known that there has to be more&nbsp;
than one Chucky. Andy figures it out before we as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:09.840 --> 00:11:13.760
the audience know. I explain this in full&nbsp;
detail in my Andy Barclay Horror History.

00:11:13.760 --> 00:11:17.280
Speaking of Andy, he’s on his way to the&nbsp;
asylum to try to save Nica and the others,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:17.280 --> 00:11:20.160
and he receives a strange call from… someone.

00:11:20.160 --> 00:11:25.680
– [Tiffany] Tiffany… Jennifer… even I lose track.

00:11:25.680 --> 00:11:29.520
– She leaves a one word clue from Chucky, and&nbsp;
Andy is supposed to know the meaning of it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.520 --> 00:11:33.680
The word is “disembowel”. Andy’s plan is to&nbsp;
hide his gun inside the short haired Chucky&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:33.680 --> 00:11:37.920
to get it into Harrogate, and disembowel&nbsp;
him to get it back once inside. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:37.920 --> 00:11:42.160
Chucky and Tiffany don’t know that. So what’s&nbsp;
the deal here? This part has always confused me.

00:11:42.160 --> 00:11:45.200
The best sense I can make of it is&nbsp;
that Chucky was threatening Andy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:45.200 --> 00:11:49.440
basically implying that he plans to disembowel&nbsp;
him, and it’s just an ironic coincidence that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:49.440 --> 00:11:53.200
Andy turns the tables on him. If anyone&nbsp;
has a better explanation, let me know.

00:11:53.200 --> 00:11:57.120
Also, when he does break open the Chucky doll,&nbsp;
we can see all the brains and guts and stuff,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:57.120 --> 00:12:00.720
even though this Chucky doll has only been&nbsp;
alive for like under an hour. It seems like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:00.720 --> 00:12:04.720
the amount of time it takes for Chucky to turn&nbsp;
human can be really inconsistent. For reference,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:04.720 --> 00:12:09.120
in Child's Play 2, it takes about 48 hours for&nbsp;
Chucky to turn human after being reincarnated,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:09.120 --> 00:12:11.520
but in Curse, he doesn’t turn&nbsp;
human for the entire movie.

00:12:11.520 --> 00:12:14.080
But let’s get back on topic. Dr. Foley. He’s about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:14.080 --> 00:12:16.880
to give some kind of treatment&nbsp;
to Claire when he says this.

00:12:16.880 --> 00:12:19.680
– [Dr. Foley] Hey how’s Jake?
– [Carlos] He’s hanging in there. Thanks.

00:12:19.680 --> 00:12:24.240
– [Zac] The next Chucky installment would be the Chucky TV&nbsp;
series, where a character named Jake Wheeler loses&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:24.240 --> 00:12:27.760
both of his parents. My first thought here&nbsp;
was that Carlos somehow knows Jake Wheeler,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:27.760 --> 00:12:31.680
and Dr. Foley is asking how Jake is holding&nbsp;
up after the death of his father. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:31.680 --> 00:12:35.440
after spending all day trying to piece together&nbsp;
the timeline using the new information from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:35.440 --> 00:12:39.360
Season 1, I think maybe it’s possible that he was&nbsp;
asking about Jake’s mother, who would have died&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:39.360 --> 00:12:41.637
two years before Cult, in 2015. 

00:12:41.637 --> 00:12:46.080
If you're confused at all about the Chucky timeline, watch this video where I explain all of it.

00:12:46.080 --> 00:12:49.920
Of course, another possibility is that Dr.&nbsp;
Foley is asking about a different person&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:49.920 --> 00:12:54.160
named Jake. And I agree that that is the easy&nbsp;
explanation, but it doesn’t account for this part,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:54.160 --> 00:12:57.840
where Chucky knocks out Dr. Foley and tries&nbsp;
to get Nica to finish him off with the bottle.

00:12:57.840 --> 00:12:59.360
– [Nica] I’m not a killer.

00:12:59.360 --> 00:13:03.200
– This is part of a different voodoo ritual where&nbsp;
Chucky’s aim is to corrupt an innocent and get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:03.200 --> 00:13:06.880
them to kill. In other words, Jake Wheeler&nbsp;
wasn’t the first one he tried to corrupt,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:06.880 --> 00:13:10.880
it was actually Nica. At the very least,&nbsp;
this proves that Don Mancini kind of knew&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:10.880 --> 00:13:14.240
what was going to happen in Season 1&nbsp;
at the time he made Cult. So it’s not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:14.240 --> 00:13:18.400
out of the question that Dr. Foley was&nbsp;
actually asking Carlos about our Jake.

00:13:18.400 --> 00:13:22.480
Also, the actor that plays Dr. Foley is&nbsp;
Michel Therriault. He also plays Lexi’s dad,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:22.480 --> 00:13:25.680
Nathan Cross in the TV series. It’s&nbsp;
definitely a different character,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:25.680 --> 00:13:28.800
so maybe the character he plays in&nbsp;
the series is a relative of Dr. Foley,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:28.800 --> 00:13:32.160
which would further connect these two&nbsp;
communities. But that's just speculation.

00:13:32.160 --> 00:13:34.800
However, since Chucky is unable&nbsp;
to get Nica to kill for him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:34.800 --> 00:13:37.200
he does the next best thing&nbsp;
and takes over her body.

00:13:37.200 --> 00:13:40.240
And this obviously leads into the&nbsp;
events of Season 1, but first,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:40.240 --> 00:13:43.680
we gotta talk about that post-credits scene.&nbsp;
For the first time since Child’s Play 2,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:43.680 --> 00:13:47.200
we see Andy’s former foster sister Kyle,&nbsp;
and when she appears, she’s wearing the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:47.200 --> 00:13:51.040
same hat and outfit that we saw her in&nbsp;
when she first appeared in that movie.

00:13:51.040 --> 00:13:53.440
Chucky and Tiffany do leave the hospital. But…

00:13:53.440 --> 00:13:56.720
– [Nica] He’ll come back. He always comes back.

00:13:57.360 --> 00:14:01.920
– [Zac] And so will I. In the next Chucky episode of&nbsp;
Things You Missed, where I’ll be covering Season&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:01.920 --> 00:14:06.880
1 of the Chucky TV series. Remember to subscribe&nbsp;
to CZsWorld for new horrors every week, RING the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:06.880 --> 00:14:12.984
deathbell and select all notifications and I will&nbsp;
see you in the next one. Assuming we both survive.

00:14:13.469 --> 00:14:15.469
(spooky dance music)

